> Good to know: A candidate who passes while no interview day is open for their role is invited but waits: the invitation email goes when you add (or open) a day for that role. The Hiring page shows "N applicants invited but no interview day is open for" the role, with **Add an interview day**. Candidates who already had the email, or opened their link and found no time ("No call times are open right now"), get "New times are open" when the day is added.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Candidates apply on carmacars.ca/careers. Every application is scored on the server against the role&#39;s rubric: a candidate who passes gets a link to book a 15-minute call, one who does not qualify for Field staff is offered Sales instead, and the rest wait for you. During each call you fill in a rubric; the final score ranks everyone in the role.</p><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-open-a-role-and-send-the-apply-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Open a role and send the apply link</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Roles and links.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Open the role</b> to put it on carmacars.ca/careers (and in the sitemap and the footer); <b class="gd-ui">Close the role</b> takes it off. Field staff, Sales in person and Remote sales start open; the three remote assistant roles start closed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Copy the apply link: it ends with ?src=indeed (or ?src=onlinejobs for the remote roles), so each application records where it came from.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Copy the message under it and paste it into Indeed (or OnlineJobs.ph) messages to each applicant. It asks them to answer the role&#39;s questions, about five minutes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Pass mark and pay</b> changes the pass mark (60 of 100 unless you change it) and the pay shown on the page.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-what-happens-to-each-application" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What happens to each application</h2><p class="gd-p">The database scores the answers the moment they arrive. The candidate never sees the points.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Score at or above the pass mark, no knock-out: an email with a personal link to book a call (Invited).</li><li>Field staff who do not qualify (no full G licence, under three years of driving, or a low score) are not declined: they get a friendly email offering Sales in person, with a one-click link that fills in their details, and Remote sales named as the other choice (Referred). If they already applied for Sales, nothing is sent and a note says so.</li><li>Sales in person below the pass mark, or remote only, is offered Remote sales. A remote assistant role below the pass mark is offered the closest other open role.</li><li>A knock-out with no other role to offer (for example the finance code word missing) gets a polite decline.</li><li>Anyone else waits for you as Below the bar, with only a confirmation email.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-review-the-applications" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review the applications</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Applications.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Filter by role, status, source (Indeed, OnlineJobs.ph, website, referral) or score. Open a candidate for every answer with the points it earned and any knock-out.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Invite anyway</b> sends the booking link to a candidate below the bar, declined or referred. <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> sends the polite decline email (untick it to decline without an email).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A candidate referred to another role shows the link both ways under Linked applications.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-interview-days" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Interview days</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Interview days.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add an interview day</b>: the day, from and to (Toronto time), the call length (15 minutes) and the break between calls (5 minutes), phone or video, and the roles it is for (empty: every role).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Phone: you call the candidate on the number they gave. Video: every booking gets its own Jitsi Meet link, in the candidate&#39;s email and on their page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Candidates book, move or cancel from their link. They get a confirmation, a reminder the evening before and one an hour before (and a text, when phone and texts are on). Remote roles show Manila time too.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> stops new bookings on a day; a day with bookings cannot be deleted.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-run-the-calls-with-the-rubric" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Run the calls with the rubric</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Calls.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Pick the day. Each call shows the time, the candidate, Call (or the video link). Press <b class="gd-ui">Start</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The rubric sits beside the call guide (what to ask each minute, and what a good answer sounds like). Score each line 1 to 5: Communication, Reliability and availability, Role skills, Customer or sales instinct, Judgement on the scenarios, Attitude.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the decision (Hire, Maybe, No, No show), add notes and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rubric</b>. The interview score (of 100) and the final score (40% screening, 60% interview) fill in, with the rank in the role.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-shortlist-and-hire" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Shortlist and Hire</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Shortlist.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each role lists its interviewed candidates by final score, rank 1 first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open the candidate and press <b class="gd-ui">Hire</b>. It invites them into the right portal: field staff, or the assistant portal (both sales roles are the Sales function, with in person or remote recorded).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Then press <b class="gd-ui">Send the agreement to sign</b>: check the values and send the staff agreement to sign in their portal.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Not hired</b> closes a candidate after the call without an email; <b class="gd-ui">Withdrawn</b> is for one who no longer wants the role.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Applications are for Admins only. The name, contact details and answers of a candidate who is not hired are deleted 12 months after the decision, as the privacy policy says.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A candidate who passes while no interview day is open for their role is invited but waits: the invitation email goes when you add (or open) a day for that role. The Hiring page shows &quot;N applicants invited but no interview day is open for&quot; the role, with <b class="gd-ui">Add an interview day</b>. Candidates who already had the email, or opened their link and found no time (&quot;No call times are open right now&quot;), get &quot;New times are open&quot; when the day is added.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'academy', 'chapter', 'hiring', null, 'Academy', 'Training paths by function: progress, opening a section early, editing lessons and questions, the gate.',
  'Training for every staff function: paths of sections, lessons played and narrated in the browser (no video files are stored), and a quiz per section.

## Progress by staff member

1. Open **People** > **Academy**. Each staff member shows their paths, sections passed and the last quiz. Settings > Staff shows the same count in its Academy column.
2. Open a person: each section with lessons watched, best score, attempts and its state.
3. A section closed for them? Press **Open early**, give the reason and press **Open early** again. The reason is kept.

## Edit lessons and questions

1. Under Paths and sections, open a section. Changes apply at once for everyone.
2. **Edit the title** changes its name and what it covers.
3. Each lesson has **Preview** (the player) and **Edit the lesson**: the title and the scenes. A scene is a caption, the words the voice says, and its picture: a title, a chat between the renter and you, a list, steps, money rows or a rule.
4. **Add a lesson**, **Delete** a lesson; each question has **Edit** (the question, the options, the right answer counted from 0, and why) and **Delete**; **Add a question** at the end.

## The pass mark and the gate

- Settings > Program: Academy: pass mark of a quiz (80% by default).
- Academy gate (off by default): off, the academy only records progress. On, a staff member who has not passed every path of their functions opens only the academy, the guide and their profile. Admins are never held.
- Take the Admin path yourself from **Take the Admin path**.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Training for every staff function: paths of sections, lessons played and narrated in the browser (no video files are stored), and a quiz per section.</p><section class="gd-task" id="academy-progress-by-staff-member" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Progress by staff member</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Academy</b>. Each staff member shows their paths, sections passed and the last quiz. Settings &gt; Staff shows the same count in its Academy column.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open a person: each section with lessons watched, best score, attempts and its state.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A section closed for them? Press <b class="gd-ui">Open early</b>, give the reason and press <b class="gd-ui">Open early</b> again. The reason is kept.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-edit-lessons-and-questions" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Edit lessons and questions</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Under Paths and sections, open a section. Changes apply at once for everyone.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Edit the title</b> changes its name and what it covers.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each lesson has <b class="gd-ui">Preview</b> (the player) and <b class="gd-ui">Edit the lesson</b>: the title and the scenes. A scene is a caption, the words the voice says, and its picture: a title, a chat between the renter and you, a list, steps, money rows or a rule.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a lesson</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Delete</b> a lesson; each question has <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> (the question, the options, the right answer counted from 0, and why) and <b class="gd-ui">Delete</b>; <b class="gd-ui">Add a question</b> at the end.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-the-pass-mark-and-the-gate" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The pass mark and the gate</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Settings &gt; Program: Academy: pass mark of a quiz (80% by default).</li><li>Academy gate (off by default): off, the academy only records progress. On, a staff member who has not passed every path of their functions opens only the academy, the guide and their profile. Admins are never held.</li><li>Take the Admin path yourself from <b class="gd-ui">Take the Admin path</b>.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'academy', 'chapter', 'commissions', null, 'Academy', 'Your training path: lessons narrated by your browser, a quiz per section, 80% to pass.',
  'Your training path is under **My work** > **Academy** (field work: **Field work** > **Academy**). There is a path for each of your functions: customer service, fleet, finance, Sales in person or remote, field work.

## Watch the lessons

1. Open **Academy**. Each path lists its sections in order, with Passed, Open or Pass the one before.
2. Open a section. Each lesson is a short video made by your browser: scenes with captions, read aloud by your browser''s own voice.
3. Press **Play**. **Pause**, **Back** and **Next** move through the scenes; **Replay** starts again; Speed goes from 0.75x to 1.5x. **Voice on** turns the voice off and on.
4. No sound or no English voice on your device? The lesson plays with captions only, each scene timed for reading.

> Tip: Use headphones in the office. The voice is your browser''s, so it can sound different on another device.

## Pass the quiz

1. Under the lessons, answer every question and press **Check my answers**.
2. You need 80% (the pass mark in Program settings). Passed: the next section opens. Not yet: each answer shows the right one and why; press **Try again** as often as you need.
3. A section that is on two of your paths (the policies, for example) counts on both once passed.

> Good to know: An Admin can open a section early for you, for example when you already did this work somewhere else. If the academy gate is on, the rest of the portal waits until you pass your paths; the guide and your profile stay open.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Your training path is under <b class="gd-ui">My work</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Academy</b> (field work: <b class="gd-ui">Field work</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Academy</b>). There is a path for each of your functions: customer service, fleet, finance, Sales in person or remote, field work.</p><section class="gd-task" id="academy-watch-the-lessons" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Watch the lessons</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Academy</b>. Each path lists its sections in order, with Passed, Open or Pass the one before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open a section. Each lesson is a short video made by your browser: scenes with captions, read aloud by your browser&#39;s own voice.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Play</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Pause</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Back</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Next</b> move through the scenes; <b class="gd-ui">Replay</b> starts again; Speed goes from 0.75x to 1.5x. <b class="gd-ui">Voice on</b> turns the voice off and on.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">No sound or no English voice on your device? The lesson plays with captions only, each scene timed for reading.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Use headphones in the office. The voice is your browser&#39;s, so it can sound different on another device.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-pass-the-quiz" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pass the quiz</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Under the lessons, answer every question and press <b class="gd-ui">Check my answers</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">You need 80% (the pass mark in Program settings). Passed: the next section opens. Not yet: each answer shows the right one and why; press <b class="gd-ui">Try again</b> as often as you need.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A section that is on two of your paths (the policies, for example) counts on both once passed.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>An Admin can open a section early for you, for example when you already did this work somewhere else. If the academy gate is on, the rest of the portal waits until you pass your paths; the guide and your profile stay open.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'academy', 'chapter', 'my-hours-and-pay', null, 'Academy', 'Your training: watch the lessons on your phone, pass each quiz.',
  'Your training path is under **Field work** > **Academy**: the handover, the return, cash and signing in the field, and the rules of the trip.

1. Open **Academy** and the first open section.
2. Press **Play** on each lesson: scenes with captions, read aloud by your phone''s own voice. **Pause**, **Back**, **Next**, **Replay** and Speed work as on a video. No voice on your phone? The captions play by themselves.
3. Answer the quiz and press **Check my answers**. 80% passes and opens the next section; **Try again** as often as you need.

> Tip: Nothing is downloaded: the lessons work on mobile data and use very little of it.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Your training path is under <b class="gd-ui">Field work</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Academy</b>: the handover, the return, cash and signing in the field, and the rules of the trip.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Academy</b> and the first open section.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Play</b> on each lesson: scenes with captions, read aloud by your phone&#39;s own voice. <b class="gd-ui">Pause</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Back</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Next</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Replay</b> and Speed work as on a video. No voice on your phone? The captions play by themselves.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Answer the quiz and press <b class="gd-ui">Check my answers</b>. 80% passes and opens the next section; <b class="gd-ui">Try again</b> as often as you need.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Nothing is downloaded: the lessons work on mobile data and use very little of it.</div></aside>');
